(Summary, written by PutiaCNC)
(Spindle (!):            Not run by the program: it stops -M0- to ask you to start it at the)
(                        speed shown, and again before a tool change and at the end to stop it.)
(                        There is no work coordinate system: jog to the zero of the job and set)
(                        it with G92 X0 Y0 Z0 first.)
(Tools:                  6 mm flat end mill, 2 mm flat end mill. No tool change.)
(Pauses:                 The program stops 4 times with the spindle off: 'Start the spindle at)
(                        10000 rpm, then resume', 'Stop the spindle and change tool to 2 mm,)
(                        then touch off Z 0 and resume', 'Start the spindle at 12000 rpm, then)
(                        resume', 'Stop the spindle, then resume'. Resume it when you are)
(                        ready; the spindle starts again by itself.)
(Cutting:                Down to Z -4 mm. 2399 mm of cutting, about 4 min 3 s in all.)
(End:                    Lifts to Z 5 mm, goes to X0 Y0.)
; PutiaCNC - Marlin (no spindle control)
; Stock 100 x 80 x 10 mm; XY0 = lower-left corner of stock, Z0 = top surface
